<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady, soyoil firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady, soyoil firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Arrivals was around 3,000 tonnes in the markets of central India which was around 20,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose by 300 rupees per tonne on tight supply from plants and refineries against good demand. Business volume was very limited and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $281-282 per tonne for export. Rapeseed extraction was $127-128 per tonne for ready shipment and for $117-118 per tonne for March/April shipment for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,350 rupees f.o.r Bedibunder and was 4,300 rupees f.o.r Bhavnagar. The undertone was steady.</p>
